From: RNSBox <rnsbox@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: dts: sophgo: enable Ethernet on the LicheeRV Nano B

The LicheeRV Nano E/WE edition wires the SG2002 internal 10/100 EPHY to
the RJ45 magjack (EPHY_TX/RX pairs through AC coupling); there is no
external MAC/PHY on the board.  The TMI7003C next to the SoC is the
3-channel DCDC+LDO power regulator, not an Ethernet device: its EN1/2/3
pins are strapped to VSYS and it has no software control interface, so
it needs no driver.

The mainline sg2002-licheerv-nano-b.dts never enabled gmac0 or the MDIO
mux, so eth0 was missing even though the DWMAC and internal-PHY support
is already present in the SoC dtsi.  Enable both, mirroring what the
Milk-V Duo S DTS does for the same EPHY on SG2000.

--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2002-licheerv-nano-b.dts
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2002-licheerv-nano-b.dts
@@ -32,6 +32,14 @@
 	clock-frequency = <25000000>;
 };
 
+&gmac0 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&mdio {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &pinctrl {
 	uart0_cfg: uart0-cfg {
 		uart0-pins {
-- 
